# 20. HARMLESS PROOF-OF-CONCEPT

In a controlled training application specifically designed for XSS practice, a tester may use a harmless browser-side proof of concept to confirm script execution.

For example, a training lab may use a simple JavaScript alert demonstration.

The important lesson is:

```text
Input
  ↓
HTML/DOM processing
  ↓
Browser interprets it as code
  ↓
Harmless proof of execution
```

Do not test this against real websites or users without explicit authorization.

