# 🎯 ONE-LINE EXAM ANSWER

> **Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) is a web application injection vulnerability in which untrusted content is improperly handled and interpreted by a user's browser, with major types being reflected, stored, and DOM-based XSS; prevention relies primarily on context-appropriate output encoding, supported by safe DOM practices, CSP, secure cookies, validation, and secure development.**